        <item>
            <title>2.35.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:24:14 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>121</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.35.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Live mirror to iPhone** — Settings › Mobile › Live mirror (off by default). When on, Canopy listens on this Mac's Tailscale address, password-checked, and shows the state there; with no Tailscale address it does not listen and says why. *Copy Connection for iPhone* puts the connection string on the clipboard. Paste it into Canopy Mobile's Settings, and any session in the phone's roster from this Mac gets a **Live** button that opens the same conversation Canopy is showing. Prompts, permission dialogs and questions work from either side, and a dialog already open when the phone connects is shown to it. Traffic goes directly over Tailscale, not through the relay.
- **Reset Password** — locks out every connection string copied before it.

### Notes

- Needs the Canopy Mobile build with Live support (Canopy-Mobile `main` at or after #52) and Tailscale on both devices.
- Anyone on your tailnet holding the connection string can read and drive this Mac's sessions until the password is reset; the Settings footer says so.
- The Mac and the phone are one session to Claude Code: a `/clear` typed on either side clears the conversation for both.
]]></description>
